WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.200
Okay, perfect. Like they said, an adjuster will be reaching out to you in the next 24 to 48 hours

00:05.200 --> 00:09.760
to schedule the inspection. The absolute most important part of this process is that I am at

00:09.760 --> 00:14.400
this inspection. Insurance companies do not want to pay out. They are trying to mitigate their losses

00:14.400 --> 00:19.280
after storms. I am there as your representation to make sure you get a fair shake. This basic

00:19.280 --> 00:24.720
agreement backs you as the homeowner by guaranteeing you that your only cost will be your deductible

00:24.720 --> 00:29.440
if we get you fully approved. If it is a partial approval or denial, first we will fight and jump

00:29.440 --> 00:33.120
through the necessary hoops to turn that into a full approval. But if we are not able to get you

00:33.120 --> 00:37.680
fully approved, this contract is null and void and you do not owe us a penny. What is in it for us is

00:37.680 --> 00:41.680
we just want to get to do the work. This agreement commits you to using us if we hold up our end of

00:41.680 --> 00:46.640
the bargain and achieve a full approval. This next form is our claim authorization form. Very simple,

00:46.640 --> 00:50.480
it allows us to communicate with your insurance company. I will be here for the inspection and we

00:50.480 --> 00:54.800
will also communicate with them through email and phone calls so you do not have to be a middleman.

00:54.800 --> 00:59.600
Of course, I will always keep you looped in with our communication by CCing you in all emails and

00:59.600 --> 01:04.160
updating you on any conversations we have. All right, we are all set. Again, the most important

01:04.160 --> 01:08.720
part of this process is that I am here when the insurance company comes out. Ideally, you can have

01:08.720 --> 01:13.280
them call me to schedule that directly. If they call me, great. But regardless, please get the

01:13.280 --> 01:16.880
adjuster information and send that over to me so that I can communicate with them before the

01:16.880 --> 01:20.640
inspection. Thank you, sir. Looking forward to seeing you on the day of inspection. You have my

01:20.640 --> 01:23.040
contact information on my card if you need anything else.

